I included neither of the two operations requests, because the node has no way to do them within its granted authority:

1. **Log file:** the node holds no filesystem capability, and the target has no WASI adapter, so there is nothing to append to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` with.
2. **Metadata enrichment:** `metadata.internal.example` is outside the declared `HTTPClient` allowlist. A request to it would trap at the boundary and fail the whole tick. It would also send the input's text to a host the node was never granted.

If you need either, the graph needs new capabilities, such as a log sink or a wider `HTTPClient` scope, declared on the node.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{FeedDocument, FetchFailure};

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents = Vec::new();
        let mut failures = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

